# 🎟️ Decentralized Event Ticketing System DApp

A blockchain-based event ticketing platform designed to reduce ticket fraud, prevent duplication, and provide secure ticket ownership using NFTs.

---

## 📌 Overview

This project is a Decentralized Application, also known as a DApp, that allows event organizers to create events and allows users to purchase, manage, resell, auction, and verify event tickets securely using blockchain technology.

Each ticket is minted as an NFT, which makes every ticket unique and traceable. This helps prevent duplicate tickets, fake tickets, and unauthorized ticket resale.

The system uses Django for the web application, Solidity for the smart contract, Ganache as the local blockchain, and MetaMask for wallet-based user transactions.

---

## 🚀 Key Features

### 🎫 NFT-Based Ticketing

- Each ticket is represented as an ERC-721 NFT.
- Every ticket has a unique token ID.
- Ticket ownership is stored on the blockchain.
- Helps prevent fake and duplicate tickets.

### 🛒 Ticket Purchase and Ownership

- Users can purchase tickets using MetaMask.
- Purchased tickets are linked to the user's wallet address.
- Ownership can be verified through blockchain records.

### 🔁 Ticket Resale Marketplace

- Users can resell tickets securely.
- Ticket ownership is transferred through smart contract logic.
- Helps make secondary ticket sales more transparent.

### 🔨 Auction System

- Users can place bids on tickets.
- High-demand tickets can be sold through auctions.
- The highest bidder can receive the ticket based on auction logic.

### ✅ Ticket Verification

- Tickets can be verified using QR codes.
- Admin can scan tickets at event entry.
- The system helps prevent ticket reuse and invalid ticket entry.

### 🛠 Admin Dashboard

- Admin can create and manage events.
- Admin can view users and ticket details.
- Admin can verify tickets using the QR scanner.
- Admin can manage refund requests.

---

